From 5d357962ccd023e16bffd5f1a2e474b560853cb7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stephan Sundermann <stephansundermann@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 12:49:50 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] [webOS] Always respond to screensaver requests with a
 timestamp

webOS 4 does not send a "state" field in the screensaver about-to-start
request, so Kodi never acknowledged it and the TV screensaver kicked in
during playback. Respond whenever the request carries a timestamp.

Fixes #30100

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit c4b1f4eb2550d625f29a7f29adb3bc276f926c4a)
---
 xbmc/windowing/wayland/OSScreenSaverWebOS.cpp | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/xbmc/windowing/wayland/OSScreenSaverWebOS.cpp b/xbmc/windowing/wayland/OSScreenSaverWebOS.cpp
index 3ae0dcb..c3dc8e0 100644
--- a/xbmc/windowing/wayland/OSScreenSaverWebOS.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/windowing/wayland/OSScreenSaverWebOS.cpp
@@ -74,7 +74,7 @@ bool COSScreenSaverWebOS::OnScreenSaverAboutToStart(LSHandle* sh, LSMessage* rep
 
   CLog::LogF(LOGDEBUG, "Responded {}", msg);
 
-  if (request["state"] != "Active")
+  if (!request.isMember("timestamp"))
     return true;
 
   CVariant response;
-- 
